# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
#
# What never reaches the docker build context. Both stages copy whole trees
# (`COPY . .` in the Go stage, `COPY ui/ ui/` in the UI stage), so anything left
# in here is uploaded to the daemon on every build and baked into a layer.
#
# node_modules is the reason this file now exists: a pnpm store for the UI
# toolchain runs to hundreds of megabytes of content that the image builds its
# own copy of anyway, and shipping it into the context would make every
# `docker build` slower for everyone, including the people who never touch the
# UI.
node_modules/

# Build output from the host. internal/adminui/dist is excluded on purpose and
# not by oversight: the UI stage produces it and the Go stage copies it from
# there, so keeping the host's copy out means the image can only ever serve the
# bundle this build made. A developer with a stale local dist gets the same
# image as CI does.
internal/adminui/dist/
bin/
dist/
runner
mockulus
*.exe

# History, CI definitions and prose. The version is passed in as a build arg, so
# nothing in the build reads git metadata, and internal/adminui/dist is the only
# go:embed in the tree — no Go package reads a document from here.
.git/
.github/
docs/
internalDocs/

# Test and release artifacts that would otherwise ride along.
test/e2e/.artifacts/
test/load/.results/
coverage.txt
covdata/
*.out
*.test
mockulus-*.tgz
*.spdx.json
